  "system": {
    "slug": "mystaria-stage-3",
    "details": {
      "level": {
        "value": 8
      },
      "publicNotes": "<p>At Stage III, Mystaria is designated a Phantom Aspirant. A monofilament blade assembly has been implanted in her left forearm, and synthetic muscle fibers lace her entire musculature. Her third-generation phase cloak is directly integrated with her neural tissue — it now provides a defensive bonus alongside concealment. She has discarded her aeon rifle for a submachine gun optimized for close-quarters work alongside the blade. The transition is visibly unsettling; she moves with the eerie, fluid precision characteristic of full Phantoms.</p><p><strong>Sneak Attack:</strong> Mystaria deals an extra 2d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p><p><strong>Phantom Cloak (1 action, 1/encounter):</strong> Mystaria becomes Invisible and gains a +1 circumstance bonus to AC until the end of her next turn or until she makes a Strike.</p><p><strong>Neural Interface:</strong> Mystaria gains a +2 circumstance bonus to initiative rolls.</p><p><strong>Kinetic Barrier:</strong> 50 Shield HP. Recharges 15 HP per turn.</p>",
      "privateNotes": "",
      "publication": {
        "title": "Mass Effect Compendium",
        "authors": "nscarpinatodev",
        "license": "ORC",
        "remaster": true
